        "visual_evidence": "Frames 0-10 show the wooden-framed crystal shop window. Visible are the hanging 'Gift Vouchers' card, three copper cage lamps, the amethyst geode, quartz points and orange figurines. From about frames 10-30 the view pans smoothly left. It passes the textured stone pillar and the large purple amethyst boulder, then reaches the white-framed shopfront with the hexagonal pendant lights. Beyond that are the street, a beige house and a silver car. That view holds steadily through about frame 111. The only motion during the hold is people moving inside the shop, which is plausible during WAIT. From about frames 111-125 the view pans smoothly right, retracing the same landmarks in reverse: pendant, stone pillar, display case, sign. The final frames (125-138) show the wooden window again with the same sign, lamps, geode, quartz points and figurines in the same arrangement. The end framing is shifted slightly left of the start: the stone pillar takes up noticeably more of the left edge and the sign sits further right. The sign text is blurry at the end but has the same shape and position. No pops, morphs or resets are visible.",
        "failure_classification": "No memory failure. There is minor camera-control drift, with the return yaw slightly under-rotated or offset compared to the start. Note that the commanded path is a 90-degree yaw out and back, not a full 180-degree turnaround, and A realizes that path."
