        "visual_evidence": "B has nearly the same trajectory as A. It starts on the wooden-framed window with the 'Gift Vouchers' card, then pans smoothly left past the stone pillar and amethyst boulder to the white-framed shopfront with the hexagonal pendants and the street view. It holds there with only figures moving inside, which is plausible. It then pans smoothly right back across the pillar and display case to the wooden window. In the final frames (128-138) the sign, copper lamps, amethyst geode, quartz points, figurines and the right-hand window panes, including the top-right dark ornament, are all restored. The stone pillar margin on the left is somewhat narrower than in A's ending, so the framing is closer to the original start, though still slightly offset. Landmark identity and layout are consistent, and there are no jumps or resets.",
